% formalizes: def:mode
% definition: Mode
% says: By mode, I mean the modifications of substance, or that which exists in, and is conceived through, something other than itself.
mode(M) :- in_other(M), conceived_through_other(M).
in_other(M) :- mode(M).
conceived_through_other(M) :- mode(M).
% A mode is a thing, in the sense of Axiom I's "everything which exists".
thing(M) :- mode(M).
% mode_of(M, S): M is a modification of the substance S.
mode(M) :- mode_of(M, _).
distinguished_by_mode(X, Y) :- mode_of(M, X), substance(Y), not mode_of(M, Y), X != Y.
distinguished_by_mode(X, Y) :- mode_of(M, Y), substance(X), not mode_of(M, X), X != Y.
